The EA people worry me just as much as any other disconnected from reality flight of fantasy that comes out of the youth who are extremely wealthy. They presume they know what is right, no matter what silliness they adopt. Somebody who has never had to work hard for anything other than maybe a good grade in school presuming that X is a worthy thing for "the masses" while they question what personal fulfillment one might derive from actually working the 60 hour backbreaking weeks they rattle on about. Those 60 hour weeks, in my particular case, left me with some of the accomplishments in my life I prefer to remember and often brag about. I am also silly enough that if I encountered somebody working to clean the building as I left late I looked them in the eye and thanked them for their work. Really, the clean environment, despite the mess on my desk, really did make it easier to think about things like the Frequency Synthesizer and Distribution Unit on the Phase 2b GPS satellites. So why not try to make their efforts more meaningful for them by letting them know you appreciate their work? Even absent that, they were providing for their own families with their own efforts without taking government handouts. They had a responsibility, and, they worked hard to embrace and fulfill it.

The short form of this is simple. I do not trust some elitist fugghead off in some intellectual fairyland knows what I need nearly as well as I do. Try to persuade me your ideal is better than mine. Maybe I'd take you up on it. Maybe not. It MUST be my decision else I am a your slave. THAT is UTTERLY intolerable, to the extent this does not involve directly injuring others. I feel it is intolerable to have this forced on me. And I feel it is intolerable to try to force my way on others. Every Person Is Different.

{^_^}
